libstdc++ 13 <memory_resource>: the bodies of __normal_iterator's operator++,
operator--, operator+ and operator- (bits/stl_iterator.h:1117-1342) and
polymorphic_allocator::destroy (bits/memory_resource.h:502) were dropped
(bin53): the requirements of the iterator concepts checked for
__normal_iterator<__pool_resource::_BigBlock *, ...>, while _BigBlock is
incomplete, instantiated them.  Requirements are now unevaluated operands
(cpp20_requires_expression_does_not_odr_use), also for constexpr functions
(cpp20_constexpr_function_in_requirement_not_instantiated).  g++ 13 accepts
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
